        </div>
        <p class="comparison-pricing-note">US dollars, checked 23 October 2026. Teleprompter Pal’s annual trial depends on eligibility. Prompt+’s listed one-time amount is below Teleprompter Pal’s annual amount, with a different feature bundle. Confirm the offer shown to your account before buying. <a href="#evidence">Source details.</a></p>
      </section>
      <div class="comparison-reading">
        <section id="why-pal" class="comparison-section">
          <h2>Why we’d choose Teleprompter Pal for a scripted take</h2>
          <p>Your script runs past a short free-reader limit, and the take needs a tighter opening or a square frame. Teleprompter Pal keeps the script, set-speed rehearsal, camera, playback and saved trim/crop edits together on iPhone. You can work through those stages for free.</p>
          <p>The script and original recording stay on the phone; no account is required for this local workflow. Keep the original separately from the edit, return to the saved changes later, or restore the full take. Pro adds every MP4 export and Photos, Files or Share delivery.</p>
          <p>That focused workflow is our reason to recommend Teleprompter Pal for this job. It supports iOS 18 and later, has a 1 MB text safeguard and uses a pace you set. See <a href="/guides/record-video-with-script-iphone/">recording video with a script on iPhone</a> and <a href="/pricing/">Teleprompter Pal’s plans</a>.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="comparison-section">
          <h2>Refine the take. Keep the original.</h2>
          <p>In our saved Teleprompter Pal device check, we shortened an 11.90-second original to a 7.90-second square MP4, then restored the original length and crop. The original remained available.</p>
          <dl class="comparison-proof"><div><dt>Original retained</dt><dd>11.90 seconds</dd></div><div><dt>Trimmed copy</dt><dd>7.90 seconds</dd></div><div><dt>Export checked</dt><dd>1080 × 1080 MP4</dd></div></dl>
          <p>The check also covered Photos, Files, Share Copy and reopening the edit after restarting the app. It used an internal development build. We have not performed this exact reset task in Prompt+. This evidence does not establish a comparative speed, quality or reliability advantage. <a href="/evidence/pal-device-test-summary-2026-10-19.json">Read the sanitized test record</a>.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="competitor-fit" class="comparison-section">
          <h2>When Prompt+ is the better fit</h2>
          <p>Consider Prompt+ when the reader needs to follow your speech, reflect text in a physical rig or accept a Word/PDF script. Its guides document presentation remotes, keyboards, pedals, game controllers and a second Mac or iOS device controlling the display. These are developer claims, not our hardware or voice-accuracy results.</p>
          <p>Its one-time reader upgrade may suit someone avoiding a recurring subscription. Prompt+ also documents a local mode that skips login. Logging in adds script sharing across devices and with its separate video app. Teleprompter Pal’s local workflow also needs no account; that is a shared benefit.</p>
          <p>Current release history advertises AI writing and rewriting, whose service availability and gates we have not tested. Prompt+ documents Zoom use on supported iPads and Macs; its platform table does not promise that workflow on iPhone. Teleprompter Pal remains focused on iPhone recording and saved video edits.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="editions" class="comparison-section">
          <h2>Prompt+ is separate from Teleprompter for Video</h2>
          <p>The US listing identifies Prompt+ Teleprompter by Norton Five Ltd, app 1483052809. Its website terms name Teleprompter For Video Ltd as operator. The sibling <a href="/compare/teleprompter-for-video-alternative/">Teleprompter for Video comparison</a> covers a separate app, ID 1139307843. Its recording or caption features do not become Prompt+ entitlements.</p>
          <p>The developer’s physical-rig guide describes Prompt+ as a reader with no video. Its remote-control guide also includes a generic recording-button label. We have not confirmed an installed camera flow, so recording, video delivery and exact video editing/reset tasks stay unverified here. A button label or shared script account does not resolve that question.</p>
          <p>Teleprompter Pal uses a pace you set in the reviewed implementation. We have not verified its physical mirror-rig task; a mirrored selfie preview is a different thing. We do not claim that either product’s voice recognition, remote connection, privacy or reliability is better without a suitable common test.</p>
        </section>
        <section class="comparison-section">
          <h2>Try the reader and the recording job separately</h2>
          <p>Start with the same script under 750 characters. Use the <a href="/tools/speech-time-calculator/">speech time calculator</a> to choose a starting pace. Read with a pause and a repeated sentence. In Prompt+, try its documented voice mode and any remote or mirror setup you need. Then check what happens with your longer script.</p>
          <p>In Teleprompter Pal, record a take, trim the opening, choose a square crop, close and reopen the edit, and restore its full length and framing. Note the Pro boundary before exporting. If your Prompt+ edition offers built-in recording, verify that route before attempting the same video task; a separate camera recording is a different setup.</p>
          <p>This is a proposed evaluation, not a matched test we completed. We have not installed and tested Prompt+’s current reader, camera, recognition, remote controls or eligible purchase sheet. Source inspection does not perform those tasks.</p>
        </section>
        <section id="evidence" class="comparison-section comparison-evidence">
          <h2>Sources and testing</h2>
          <p>We make Teleprompter Pal. This comparison separates saved internal device evidence, current source/offer inspection and documented developer claims. Conflicting or incomplete evidence stays unverified.</p>
          <ul class="comparison-source-list">
            <li><strong>Teleprompter Pal device checks, 19 October 2026.</strong> iPhone 17 Pro, iOS 27.0, Teleprompter Pal 0.6.17 (37), development-signed builds. The <a href="/evidence/pal-device-test-summary-2026-10-19.json">sanitized record</a> covers the stated edit and delivery task. It does not certify a current public App Store binary.</li>
            <li><strong>Teleprompter Pal offer and relevant iPhone source.</strong> Inspected 23 October 2026 for local creation, set-speed reading, the 1 MB text safeguard and every-delivery Pro gate. This is source inspection, not a new device test.</li>
            <li><strong>Apple US listing and lookup: Prompt+ Teleprompter.</strong> Norton Five Ltd, app 1483052809, version 11.4.6, iOS 14+, checked 23 October 2026. Sources for the free cap, purchase listing and feature/release descriptions; no eligible checkout test.</li>
            <li><strong>Prompt+ official website, contact FAQ and Terms of Use.</strong> Checked 23 October 2026; terms last updated 19 May 2026. Sources for skip-login local use, logged-in sharing, one-time renewal terms and possible future-service charges. The homepage and Zoom guide distinguish supported iPad/Mac presentation use; the current store minimum governs over the older guide.</li>
            <li><strong>Developer guides: Using the app in a physical teleprompter; Remote controls.</strong> Checked 23 October 2026. The first explicitly distinguishes Prompt+ and Teleprompter for Video and describes Prompt+ without video. The second documents controls but includes a generic recording label. These do not establish an installed capture test; video-workflow states remain neutral.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>
        <section class="comparison-section comparison-questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
          <h2 id="questions-title">Questions before choosing</h2>
          <details><summary>Which app is cheaper?</summary><p>Prompt+ lists a $19.99 one-time reader upgrade. Teleprompter Pal Pro costs $59.99/year, $19.99/month or $9.99/week for video export and delivery. Its one-time amount is below Teleprompter Pal’s annual amount, with a different bundle. Its current checkout and future-service inclusions need checking.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can Prompt+ record video on iPhone?</summary><p>The developer’s rig guide describes Prompt+ without video, while its remote guide includes a recording label. We have not verified an installed camera flow. Teleprompter for Video is a separate app. Teleprompter Pal’s built-in recording is free; every MP4 and Photos, Files or Share delivery requires Pro.</p></details>
          <details><summary>What can I use for free?</summary><p>Teleprompter Pal offers scripts within its 1 MB safeguard, rehearsal, recording, playback and saved trim/crop edits. Prompt+ advertises free scripts up to 750 characters, then a one-off upgrade for longer scripts. That is a script-length limit, not a recording timer or verified free-video-export offer.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Do I have to log in?</summary><p>Teleprompter Pal’s local script and recording workflow needs no account. Prompt+ also documents a Skip option for local/offline use. Its cloud script sharing requires login; offline script use does not establish offline recognition or AI availability.</p></details>
          <details><summary>Can I restore the original after editing?</summary><p>Teleprompter Pal retains its original separately; our saved internal check restored full length and crop and reopened saved edits. Prompt+’s exact recorded-video editing/reset task is untested and stays unverified.</p></details>
        </section>
